  "final_agent_text": "READY_TO_MODEL\n\nConfirmed understanding:\n\n- **Problem type:** Unrelated-parallel-machine scheduling (each batch has a different processing time on each vat), minimizing makespan.\n- **Machines:** 3 dyeing vats.\n- **Jobs:** 5 batches, all available at time 0.\n- **Assignment rule:** Each batch is assigned to exactly one vat and processed entirely there (no splitting).\n- **Sequencing:** Batches assigned to the same vat run sequentially with no overlap; no setup/changeover times, so the next batch starts immediately when the previous one finishes.\n- **No limits:** A vat may process any number of batches.\n- **No precedence:** Batches can be sequenced in any order.\n- **Objective:** Minimize the makespan (completion time of the last batch across all vats), with no other costs or penalties.\n\nProcessing time matrix (batch i, vat j):\n- Batch 1: [3, 1, 1]\n- Batch 2: [2, 1.5, 1]\n- Batch 3: [3, 1.2, 1.3]\n- Batch 4: [2, 2, 2]\n- Batch 5: [2.1, 2, 3]\n\nThe model will use binary assignment variables (batch i to vat j), continuous start-time variables, sequencing constraints (disjunctive ordering) within each vat, and a makespan variable bounded above by each batch's completion time, minimized in the objective.",
